# A2: Top-level server-tier dependencies for the dashboard backend.
#
# This file lists only the packages we depend on DIRECTLY. The fully pinned
# (hash-locked) `requirements.txt` is generated from this file by:
#
#     uv pip compile --generate-hashes requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#
# or equivalently with pip-tools (`pip-compile`). Commit BOTH files. On the
# server, install with:
#
#     pip install --require-hashes -r requirements.txt
#
# Hashes mean the install is byte-deterministic: an upstream package being
# tampered with does not silently change the deploy. Re-locking is a deliberate
# step (edit requirements.in, run `uv pip compile`, commit the new lock).
#
# Why this matters now: M3 introduced two server-tier deps that were not
# tracked here (python-multipart, hand-installed for K.0 artifact upload;
# markdown-it-py, load-bearing for K.5/K.6 HTML rendering as a transitive of
# rich). The next deploy would silently break if either disappeared. M2.5
# adds more — pinning the surface stops that class of regression.

# --- FastAPI runtime ---
fastapi
uvicorn[standard]
pydantic>=2
python-multipart
sse-starlette

# --- HTTP client ---
httpx

# --- Data layer (pandas + parquet) ---
pandas
pyarrow
# lane D1b: the NYSE calendar behind the data check's bar_on_closed_day flag
exchange_calendars==4.13.2

# --- Rendering / sanitisation ---
markdown-it-py
rich
bleach

